7.6 |\n| Financial\\tServices | 1.4 | 1.7 | 1.6 |\n| Total\\tfrom\\treportable\\tsegments | 75.3 | 51.1 | 50.3 |\n| Corporate | 0.4 | 0.8 | 1.9 |\n| Total\\tdepreciation\\tand\\tamortization | $75.7 | $51.9 | $52.2 |\n\n# Geographic\tregions:\n\n| (Amounts\tin\tmillions) | 2007 | 2006 | 2005 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Total\\trevenue:* |  |  |  |\n| United\\tStates | $1,655.0 | $1,410.1 | $1,343.2 |\n| Europe | 847.7 | 746.5 | 671.3 |\n| All\\tother | 401.5 | 347.5 | 320.1 |\n| Total\\trevenue | $2,904.2 | $2,504.1 | $2,334.6 |\n\n| (Amounts\tin\tmillions) | 2007 | 2006 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Long-lived\\tassets:** |  |  |\n| United\\tStates | $936.5 | $971.5 |\n| Sweden | 153.5 | 159.1 |\n| All\\tother | 268.4 | 200.4 |\n| Total\\tlong-lived\\tassets | $1,358.4 | $1,331.0 |\n\n* Revenue\tis\tattributed\tto\tcountries\tbased\ton\tthe\torigin\tof\tthe\tsale.\n\n** Long-lived\tassets\tconsist\tof\tProperty\tand\tequipment-net,\tGoodwill\tand\tOther\tintangibles-net.\n\nProducts\tand\tservices:\tSnap-on\tderives\tnet\tsales\tfrom\ta\tbroad\tline\tof\tproducts\tand\tcomplementary\tservices\tthat\tare\tgrouped\tinto\tthree\tcategories:\t(i)\ttools; (ii)\tdiagnostics\tand\trepair\tinformation;\tand\t(iii)\tequipment.\tThe\ttools\tcategory\tincludes\tSnap-on's\thand\ttools,\tpower\ttools,\ttool\tstorage\tunits,\tsaws,\tand\tcutting\tand pruning\ttools\tproduct\tofferings.\tThe\tdiagnostics\tand\trepair\tinformation\tcategory\tincludes\thandheld\tand\tPC-based\tdiagnostics\tproducts,\tservice\tand\trepair\tinformation products,\tdiagnostic\tsoftware\tsolutions,\tincluding\telectronic\tparts\tcatalogs,\tbusiness\tmanagement\tand\tother\n\nsolutions\tto\thelp\tdealerships\tmanage\tand\ttrack\tperformance.\tThe\tequipment\tcategory\tincludes\tsolutions\tfor\tthe\tdiagnosis\tand\tservice\tof\tautomotive\tand\tindustrial equipment.\tSnap-on\talso\tderives\trevenue\tfrom\tfinancing\tits\tproducts\tthrough\tSOC\tand\tthrough\tits\twholly\towned\tfinance\tsubsidiaries.\tSnap-on\tutilizes\tvarious financing\tprograms\tto\tfacilitate\tthe\tsales\tof\tits\tproducts.\tFurther\tproduct\tline\tinformation\tis\tnot\tpresented\tas\tit\tis\tnot\tpracticable\tto\tdo\tso.\tThe\tfollowing\ttable\tshows\tthe consolidated\tnet\tsales\tand\trevenues\tof\tthese\tproduct\tgroups\tin\tthe\tlast\tthree\tyears:\n\n| (Amounts\tin\tmillions) | 2007 | 2006 | 2005 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Net\\tsales: |  |  |  |\n| Tools | $1,632.2 | $1,453.1 | $1,387.3 |\n| Diagnostics\\tand\\trepair\\tinformation | 647.6 | 499.5 | 405.8 |\n| Equipment | 561.4 | 502.5 | 487.9 |\n| Total\\tnet\\tsales | $2,841.2 | $2,455.1 | $2,281.0 |\n| Financial\\tservices\\trevenue | 63.0 | 49.0 | 53.6 |\n| Total\\trevenue | $2,904.2 | $2,504.1 | $2,334.6 |\n\n# Note\t19:\tQuarterly\tData\t(Unaudited)\n\n|  | First | Second | Third | Fourth |  |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| (Amounts\\tin\\tmillions,\\texcept\\tper\\tshare\\tdata) | Quarter | Quarter | Quarter | Quarter | Total |\n| 2007 |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Net\\tsales | $705.7 | $711.9 | $680.7 | $742.9 | $2,841.2 |\n| Gross\\tprofit | 309.9 | 322.4 | 300.9 | 333.4 | 1,266.6 |\n| Financial\\tservices\\trevenue | 13.4 | 14.8 | 15.8 | 19.0 | 63.0 |\n| Financial\\tservices\\texpenses | (9.7) | (9.7) | (10.2) | (11.0) | (40.6) |\n| Total\\trevenue | 719.1 | 726.7 | 696.5 | 761.9 | 2,904.2 |\n| Net\\tearnings\\tfrom\\tcontinuing\\toperations | 38.0 | 52.8 | 41.1 | 57.3 | 189.2 |\n| Net\\tearnings | 39.0 | 43.8 | 41.1 | 57.3 | 181.2 |\n| Earnings\\tper\\tshare\\t–\\tbasic | 0.67 | 0.75 | 0.71 | 1.00 | 3.13 |\n| Earnings\\tper\\tshare\\t–\\tdiluted | 0.66 | 0.74 | 0.70 | 0.98 | 3.09 |\n| Cash\\tdividends\\tpaid\\tper\\tshare | 0.27 | 0.27 | 0.27 | 0.30 | 1.11 |\n| 2006 |  |  |  |  |  |\n| Net\\tsales | $587.3 | $621.7 | $594.7 | $651.4 | $2,455.1 |\n| Gross\\tprofit | 258.6 | 279.9 | 258.6 | 282.7 | 1,079.8 |\n| Financial\\tservices\\trevenue | 11.2 | 11.7 | 11.3 | 14.8 | 49.0 |\n| Financial\\tservices\\texpenses | (9.2) | (8.7) | (8.3) | (9.8) | (36.0) |\n| Total\\trevenue | 598.5 | 633.4 | 606.0 | 666.2 | 2,504.1 |\n| Net\\tearnings\\tfrom\\tcontinuing\\toperations | 21.3 | 11.7 | 27.6 | 37.3 | 97.9 |\n| Net\\tearnings | 22.1 | 11.8 | 28.2 | 38.0 | 100.1 |\n| Earnings\\tper\\tshare\\t—\\tbasic | 0.38 | 0.20 | 0.48 | 0.65 | 1.72 |\n| Earnings\\tper\\tshare\\t—\\tdiluted | 0.37 | 0.20 | 0.48 | 0.64 | 1.69 |\n| Cash\\tdividends\\tpaid\\tper\\tshare | 0.27 | 0.27 | 0.27 | 0.27 | 1.08 |\n\nNote\t–\tNet\tearnings\tin\tthe\t2006\tsecond\tquarter\tand\tfull\tyear\tincluded\ta\t$23.4\tmillion\tafter-tax\tcharge\t($0.40\tper\tdiluted\tshare)\trelated\tto\tthe\tresolution\tof\tthe\tfranchisee\tlitigation\tsettlement.\n\nPursuant\tto\tthe\trequirements\tof\tSection\t13\tor\t15(d)\tof\tthe\tSecurities\tExchange\tAct\tof\t1934,\tSnap-on\thas\tduly\tcaused\tthis\treport\tto\tbe\tsigned\ton\tits\tbehalf\tby\tthe undersigned,\tthereunto\tduly\tauthorized.\n\nNicholas\tT.\tPinchuk,\tPresident\tand\tChief\tExecutive\tOfficer\n\nPursuant\tto\tthe\trequirements\tof\tthe\tSecurities\tExchange\tAct\tof\t1934,\tthis\treport\thas\tbeen\tsigned\tbelow\tby\tthe\tfollowing\tpersons\ton\tbehalf\tof\tSnap-on\tand\tin\tthe capacities\tand\ton\tthe\tdate\tindicated.\n\nVice\tPresident\tand\tController\n\n# By: /s/\tBruce\tS.\tChelberg\n\n# Bruce\tS.\tChelberg,\tDirector\n\n| By: | /s/\tBruce\tS.\tChelberg | Date: | February\t19,\t2008 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n|  | Bruce\\tS.\\tChelberg,\\tDirector |  |  |\n| By: | /s/\\tKaren\\tL.\\tDaniel | Date: | February\\t19,\\t2008 |\n|  | Karen\\tL.\\tDaniel,\\tDirector |  |  |\n| By: | /s/\\tRoxanne\\tJ.\\tDecyk | Date: | February\\t19,\\t2008 |\n|  | Roxanne\\tJ.\\tDecyk,\\tDirector |  |  |\n| By: | /s/\\tJohn\\tF.\\tFiedler | Date: | February\\t19,\\t2008 |\n|  | John\\tF.\\tFiedler,\\tDirector |  |  |\n| By: | /s/\\tJames\\tP.\\tHolden | Date: | February\\t19,\\t2008 |\n|  | James\\tP.\\tHolden,\\tDirector |  |  |\n| By: | /s/\\tArthur\\tL.\\tKe